      "page_title": "N+1 Queries and Lazy Loading",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is N+1?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==N+1==: **1** query loads N parent rows",
            "each `parent.children` access fires one more query",
            "100 users → **101** round trips to Postgres",
            "it is invisible in code; it shows up in the SQL log"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "SELECT users",
                "sub": "1 query",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "posts WHERE user_id=1",
                "sub": "+1"
              },
              {
                "text": "posts WHERE user_id=2",
                "sub": "+1"
              },
              {
                "text": "… user_id=N",
                "sub": "+N total",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: why async breaks",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "res = await s.scalars(select(User))",
            "users = res.all()",
            "users[0].posts   # implicit lazy load",
            "# → MissingGreenlet raised"
          ],
          "note": "attribute access cannot await"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "sync Session: lazy load **silently** runs a query",
            "AsyncSession: can't `await` inside `obj.attr` → ==MissingGreenlet==",
            "fail loudly: `relationship(lazy='raise')`",
            "or `.options(raiseload('*'))` in tests"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. selectinload vs joinedload",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Loader",
            "SQL",
            "Queries",
            "Best for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`selectinload(User.posts)`",
              "`WHERE user_id IN (...)`",
              "**2** total",
              "one-to-many"
            ],
            [
              "`joinedload(Post.author)`",
              "LEFT OUTER JOIN",
              "**1**",
              "many-to-one"
            ],
            [
              "joinedload on a collection",
              "JOIN, duplicate rows",
              "1",
              "call `.unique()`"
            ],
            [
              "`awaitable_attrs.posts`",
              "lazy SELECT",
              "+1, awaited",
              "deliberate load"
            ],
            [
              "`raiseload('*')`",
              "none",
              "error",
              "tests"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Loading deliberately",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "class User(AsyncAttrs, Base):",
            "    ...",
            "ps = await u.awaitable_attrs.posts",
            "await s.refresh(u, ['posts'])"
          ],
          "note": "explicit await, no hidden query"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Keep attributes after commit",
          "text": "`async_sessionmaker(eng, expire_on_commit=False)`: loaded attributes survive **commit**, so no hidden refresh."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Mistakes and batching",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "rows = await conn.fetch(",
            "  'SELECT * FROM users'",
            "  ' WHERE id = ANY($1::int[])',",
            "  ids)  # one query, a list"
          ],
          "note": "asyncpg: pass a Python list"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`gather(*(s.get(User, i) ...))` on one session → N queries, **unsafe**",
            "Looping `fetchrow()` per id instead of one ==ANY($1)==",
            "Default `expire_on_commit` → next attribute read raises ==MissingGreenlet==",
            "joinedload on a collection without `.unique()`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "asyncio loading traps"
