      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. Why Pools Are Finite",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each connection is a ==backend process== using several MB of RAM",
            "`max_connections` defaults to **100**",
            "3 are reserved for superusers, so apps get 97",
            "More connections mean more RAM and CPU contention"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "QueuePool arg",
            "Default",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`pool_size`",
              "5",
              "kept open"
            ],
            [
              "`max_overflow`",
              "10",
              "burst extras"
            ],
            [
              "`pool_timeout`",
              "30 s",
              "wait, then error"
            ],
            [
              "`pool_recycle`",
              "-1",
              "**never** recycled"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Mechanism: Pool = Semaphore",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "In asyncio the pool works as a ==semaphore==",
            "Thousands of coroutines queue for a few connections",
            "Waiting on the pool is cheap, so a small pool is **normal**",
            "A connection is held only during a query or transaction"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "1000 coroutines",
                "sub": "awaiting checkout",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "Pool 5 + 10",
                "sub": "semaphore",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Postgres",
                "sub": "97 app slots",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Example: Size It",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# Little's law",
            "rps  = 500",
            "hold = 0.02   # s per checkout",
            "need = rps * hold   # = 10 conns"
          ],
          "note": "use hold time, not request time"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# instances × workers × (5+10)",
            "total = 3 * 4 * 15   # 180",
            "limit = 100 - 3 - 7  # headroom",
            "assert total < limit  # FAILS!"
          ],
          "note": "count max_overflow too"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "PostgreSQL wiki heuristic",
          "text": "connections ≈ (CPU cores × 2) + effective spindles. With 8 cores and 1 SSD that is about 17. A **bigger** pool often gets slower because of contention."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 4. Comparison: Pool Settings",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Setting",
            "Survives",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`pool_pre_ping=True`",
              "DB restart, firewall idle-kill",
              "1 round trip per checkout"
            ],
            [
              "`pool_recycle=1800`",
              "LB/proxy silent drops",
              "reconnect every 30 min"
            ],
            [
              "`poolclass=NullPool`",
              "PgBouncer, serverless",
              "new connect per checkout"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "eng = create_async_engine(url,",
            "  poolclass=NullPool,",
            "  connect_args={",
            "    \"statement_cache_size\": 0})"
          ],
          "note": "behind PgBouncer: it owns pooling"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "DB restarts or firewall between: `pool_pre_ping=True`",
            "LB or proxy drops idle links: set ==pool_recycle==",
            "PgBouncer or serverless: **NullPool**",
            "Timeouts at 30 s: check for leaked sessions first"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky-pink",
          "title": "Symptom",
          "text": "`TimeoutError: QueuePool limit of size 5 overflow 10 reached` after 30 s means the pool is **undersized** or sessions are leaking."
        }
      ],
