      "page_title": "aiosqlite and redis.asyncio",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. What is aiosqlite",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{icon:sqlite} ==aiosqlite== runs stdlib `sqlite3` on a **dedicated** thread per connection",
            "Its async methods proxy each call to that thread, so the loop stays free",
            "SQLite allows **one** writer at a time, which causes 'database is locked'",
            "Fix: `PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL` + `PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with aiosqlite.connect(",
            "    \"app.db\") as db:",
            "  db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row",
            "  await db.execute(sql, params)",
            "  await db.commit()  # explicit!"
          ],
          "note": "Row gives r[\"name\"] access"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. What is redis.asyncio",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{icon:redis} ==aioredis== merged into redis-py **4.2+** as `redis.asyncio`",
            "Create one `ConnectionPool.from_url(url, max_connections=50)` per app",
            "Pass it as `Redis(connection_pool=pool)`, **never** one client per request",
            "Close at shutdown: `await r.aclose()` (5.0.1+)"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "r = redis.asyncio.Redis.from_url(",
            "    url, decode_responses=True)",
            "await r.set(\"k\", \"v\", ex=60)",
            "await r.get(\"k\")      # \"v\" (str)",
            "await r.aclose()"
          ],
          "note": "decode_responses: str, not bytes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "ps = r.pubsub()",
            "await ps.subscribe(\"ch\")",
            "async for msg in ps.listen():",
            "  print(msg[\"data\"])"
          ],
          "note": "first message = subscribe confirmation"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with r.pipeline() as p:",
            "  await p.watch(\"bal\")",
            "  v = int(await p.get(\"bal\"))",
            "  p.multi()",
            "  p.set(\"bal\", v - 10)",
            "  await p.execute()  # WatchError?"
          ],
          "note": "WatchError → retry the whole block"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 4. SQLite vs Postgres",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "sqlite+aiosqlite",
            "postgresql+asyncpg"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Writers",
              "**one** at a time",
              "many (MVCC)"
            ],
            [
              "Types",
              "loose affinity",
              "strict"
            ],
            [
              "Locking",
              "whole DB file",
              "row-level"
            ],
            [
              "Best for",
              "tests, local dev",
              "production"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Test URL",
          "text": "`sqlite+aiosqlite:///app.db` is handy in tests, but a test that passes here can still **fail** on Postgres"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Calling plain `sqlite3` in a coroutine **blocks** the loop",
            "No WAL or busy_timeout → 'database is locked'",
            "Creating a Redis client per request → connection storm",
            "Ignoring `WatchError` → lost update; retry, or use an atomic ==Lua== script",
            "Skipping `aclose()` → leaked sockets at shutdown"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Lua under contention",
          "text": "WATCH retries pile up when many clients hit one key. A ==Lua== script runs **atomically** on the server: no retry loop, one round trip."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "redis",
      "subtitle": "SQLite + Redis, async"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "WAL Setup, Redis Pipelines & Pools",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with aiosqlite.connect(",
            "    \"app.db\") as db:",
            "  await db.execute(",
            "    \"PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL\")",
            "  await db.execute(",
            "    \"PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000\")"
          ],
          "note": "WAL persists; busy_timeout is per-conn"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 5. Examples: batch, subscribe, lock",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with r.pipeline(",
            "    transaction=True) as p:",
            "  p.incr(\"hits\")        # queued",
            "  p.expire(\"hits\", 60)  # queued",
            "  await p.execute()     # 1 trip"
          ],
          "note": "MULTI/EXEC: one round trip"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "ps = r.pubsub()",
            "await ps.subscribe(\"news\")",
            "m = await ps.get_message(",
            "  True, timeout=1.0)  # or None",
            "await ps.aclose()"
          ],
          "note": "True skips the subscribe confirmation"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with r.lock(\"job\",",
            "    timeout=10,",
            "    blocking_timeout=5):",
            "  await run_job()  # one worker"
          ],
          "note": "timeout frees lock if holder crashes"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 6. Setup and Shutdown",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "pool = ConnectionPool.from_url(",
            "    url, max_connections=50)",
            "r = Redis(connection_pool=pool)",
            "# ... app lifespan ...",
            "await r.aclose()",
            "await pool.disconnect()"
          ],
          "note": "a passed-in pool isn't auto-closed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 7. Which Redis Tool?",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "Use",
            "Why"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "batch commands",
              "`pipeline()`",
              "1 round trip"
            ],
            [
              "all-or-nothing group",
              "MULTI/EXEC",
              "queued, atomic"
            ],
            [
              "read-modify-write",
              "WATCH + retry",
              "==optimistic== lock"
            ],
            [
              "complex atomic step",
              "Lua script",
              "runs server-side"
            ],
            [
              "fan-out events",
              "`pubsub()`",
